{"id": "EUVD-2026-82180", "enisaUuid": "c24760a4-b97d-3e6e-9369-b88fc826e5a3", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmedia: ipu6: Do not free aux device pdata after init\n\nipu6_bus_initialize_device() stores the isys/psys pdata pointer in\nstruct ipu6_bus_device and initializes the auxiliary device. After that\npoint, error unwinding must drop the auxiliary device reference and let\nipu6_bus_release() free both the bus device and adev->pdata.\n\nThe isys and psys init paths already call put_device() when MMU\ninitialization fails, and ipu6_bus_add_device() calls\nauxiliary_device_uninit() on auxiliary_device_add() failure. Both paths\ntherefore run the bus release callback. The extra kfree(pdata) in the\ncallers can release the same object a second time.\n\nRemove the manual pdata frees after the auxiliary device has been\ninitialized.\n\nThis issue was found by a static analysis checker and confirmed by\nmanual source review.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:10:54", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:05:06", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/faa1eb97f0e66bf122f44b62be6b323f86333e9f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5323ed5a7bb2568191ec676b2035b0396105aa05", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7d102d1f0631807a491a140f67c9628dea85dfd2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9be07216af4cfc4813e1a46ce26407d31ea845de"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93070", "GHSA-2q2h-4p8v-3772"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "07e83e71-b29c-3800-a3c7-4d4324044072", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "451a02ad-6422-3f41-a353-84125169b319", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cb3117b074aefb0320d8d728a0a7f277a121adbd <5323ed5a7bb2568191ec676b2035b0396105aa05"}, {"id": "73fbabe3-accc-3784-9f2b-b9465772d21a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cb3117b074aefb0320d8d728a0a7f277a121adbd <9be07216af4cfc4813e1a46ce26407d31ea845de"}, {"id": "742bb473-8fad-30dc-90a9-44e9f571de61", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cb3117b074aefb0320d8d728a0a7f277a121adbd <7d102d1f0631807a491a140f67c9628dea85dfd2"}, {"id": "79f4f98f-af65-38b7-8a39-7def28d4b15a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "8c494e3f-75d2-3245-9d0e-bbc9a40b7c18", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "c9ec0c74-2fa7-3bcb-8ae3-3e5065f96d4f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "d0cb908c-8bf3-3c11-9cdc-2702db732892", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.10"}, {"id": "f7c5e776-02b4-3435-8483-05737a383047", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "f825854d-8216-3f7c-ba1e-2b914c14f051", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cb3117b074aefb0320d8d728a0a7f277a121adbd <faa1eb97f0e66bf122f44b62be6b323f86333e9f"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "caac1ac0-5640-3067-8f2f-97db52b1b949", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}